# Custom applications

Generated standalone apps are the right default. Switch to authored `main.roc`
when you need custom routing, extra platform effects, or a shape the
generator does not cover. Reuse `.rocci` components either way.

**Starting files:** [Datastar gallery](/examples/datastar/) (normal pattern
gallery) and [Snake](/examples/snake/) (advanced stress example).
**Verify:** `rocci run examples/rocci/custom/datastar --no-window` serves
`/search`.

## Directory apps

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run examples/rocci/custom/datastar --no-window
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/search | grep -E 'search|datastar'
```

`rocci run` on a directory compiles sibling `.rocci` modules and starts the
authored Roc program. `@get:view` / `@method:fragment` on those modules are
not the generated standalone dispatcher; `main.roc` owns HTTP.

Read the gallery source index: [datastar source](/examples/datastar/source/).

| Route | What to notice |
| --- | --- |
| `/search` | `@let`, `@if`, `@for` |
| `/edit` | `@match` for editing |
| `/todos` | filters and lists |
| `/tabs` | lazy tabs |
| `/validate` | inline validation |

The server still owns HTML. Datastar remains transport.

## Snake is the ceiling

[Snake](/examples/snake/) is an explicitly advanced multiplayer stress
example with a hand-written SSE unfold. Do not copy that unfold into ordinary
apps; generated `@get:live` already emits the poll loop. Use Snake when you
need a custom ceiling the generator does not cover.

**Related:** [Applications](/docs/applications/),
[Package](/docs/applications/package/).
